meta {
  name: Delete the question paper
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/library/{{paperItemId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  Deleting a content item is a real delete, unlike an asset, which is
  tombstoned. An item is a catalogue entry; the bytes it describes are the
  asset and they are not touched here.

  The exam metadata goes with it. question_papers cascades from its item, so
  the sidecar cannot outlive the thing it describes -- and a paper row with no
  item would be exam metadata about nothing, matched by every paper search.

  Deleting an item that a placement points at fails instead of cascading, which
  is why folder 11 removes its placements before folder 12 removes anything.
}
